 "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet gateway (multiple indoor units, P-Link/S-Link)",
 "applies_to": "Panasonic VRF, PAC and GHP systems with a U1U2 P-Link/S-Link connection.",
 "summary": "Intesis 700 Series multi-protocol gateway set up for BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP on a Panasonic U1U2 P-Link/S-Link bus. It publishes occupancy settings, gateway-wide commands, an outdoor-unit block (demand limit, pressures, compressor hours) and an indoor-unit block per unit: on/off, mode, setpoint, fan, vane, room temperature, a BMS ambient-temperature input, discharge setpoints, setpoint limits, error code, filter, remote-controller permissions, occupancy and energy consumption.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Indoor unit instance = (IU x 100) + ((L - 1) x 20000) + offset, IU 1-64; IU 1 on L = 1 is shown (100-123).",
  "Outdoor unit instance = (OU x 25) + ((L - 1) x 1000) + 10000 + offset, OU 1-30; OU 1 on L = 1 is shown (10025-10030).",
  "The manual lists LXOUXX_Demand Limit. Ratio_C with type code 0 but labels it Analog Output; it is shown as AO here.",
  "The BACnet table has no read/write column; access is inferred from object type.",
  "Consumption objects report Wh or kWh as set in Intesis MAPS.",
  "Replaces the older INBACPAN016O000/064O000 BACnet server (listed separately), which uses a different object map."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "700 Series Air Gateway IN770AIR***O000 - Panasonic Systems (U1U2 P-Link/S-Link) to Modbus, KNX, BACnet, MQTT and Home Automation - User Manual",
